#            in this order.
#
# THE BYTES ARE UPSTREAM'S BLOB BYTES, not a working-tree copy: they are LF and a Windows
# checkout of anydoc is CRLF, so `git archive` under core.autocrlf=true produces different
# files and different digests. `git cat-file blob` is the extractor, `vendor/anydoc/
# .gitattributes` carries `* -text` to keep them, and a reviewer can fetch any path below
# from raw.githubusercontent.com at the commit above and get a byte match.
#
# WHAT IS HERE: src/ (the whole Rust crate), python/ (the PyO3 binding whose `py.detach` is
# the S1 seam's warrant, 14-security.md:502), fuzz/ (the twelve cargo-fuzz targets 04:2091
# counts and the seed corpus 14:477 mirrors into fuzz/seeds/), and the five root files that
# establish the version, the dependency set and the licence.
#
# WHAT IS NOT: tests/ (2.1 MB of binary fixtures -- omniweave generates its own, see
# packages/omniweave-office/fixtures/), node/ and wasm/ (bindings omniweave does not use;
# `anydoc/wasm/LICENSE` is 14-security.md:1518's open VERIFY and stays open), bench/,
# examples/, skills/, scripts/. Excluding them is why this manifest exists: it says exactly
# which bytes the `vendored` trust tier (04:1111) was granted over.
#
# REPRODUCE
#   git -C <anydoc checkout at that commit> cat-file blob HEAD:<path>   for each path below
